speechtext:
I am supporting the item of
onions under the British preference for the same reason I voted for the budget, because it contained in a large measure other items which would be affected by the same preference. I must say that I do not approve of certain proposals contained in the budget;
I have already made myself clear on that point. My viewpoint has been confirmed by no less an authority than the leader of the opposition. It is an unexpected pleasure to find that hon. gentleman saying that prices would be raised to the consumer.
